<section class="shell band">
  <h1>Request an appointment</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Fill this in and it opens a prefilled email to the practice, which you send. Nothing is
    transmitted from this page and nothing is stored on this site. Consults are
    <strong>free</strong>: fifteen minutes for therapy, thirty for supervision or EMDR
    consultation. If you would rather write your own, the address is
    <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="note"><strong>Please do not put personal information in this form.</strong> It
  builds an ordinary email, and ordinary email is not a secure channel. No clinical detail, no
  diagnoses, no date of birth, no insurance or policy numbers, and nothing you would not want
  sitting in an inbox. Your name, a way to reach you, and a few words about what you are looking
  for is all that is needed. The rest belongs in the consult, where it is confidential.</p>
</section>

<section class="band band--night">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>What you are asking about</h2>
    <form class="request" data-request novalidate>
      <p class="prompt">
        <label for="r-name">Your name</label>
        <input id="r-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
      </p>
      <p class="prompt">
        <label for="r-email">Email</label>
        <input id="r-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required>
      </p>
      <p class="prompt">
        <label for="r-phone">Phone, if you would rather be called</label>
        <input id="r-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel">
      </p>
      <p class="prompt">
        <label for="r-service">What are you looking for?</label>
        <input id="r-service" name="service" type="text"
         placeholder="Therapy, supervision, EMDR consultation, or just &ldquo;not sure yet&rdquo;">
      </p>
      <p class="prompt">
        <label for="r-where">Where in Texas are you?</label>
        <input id="r-where" name="where" type="text" placeholder="City, or just &ldquo;online is fine&rdquo;">
      </p>
      <p class="prompt">
        <label for="r-when">Two or three times that usually work for you</label>
        <textarea id="r-when" name="when" rows="2" placeholder="Weekday mornings, or Tuesday and Thursday after 4, or whatever is true"></textarea>
      </p>
      <p class="note">A reminder before you send: no clinical detail, and nothing personal
      beyond how to reach you.</p>
      <p class="saved-hint" data-request-hint aria-live="polite"></p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <button class="cta" type="submit">Open the email, ready to send</button>
        <a class="cta cta--quiet" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email us directly</a>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>What happens next</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Someone reads it and sends times.</strong> Usually within a couple of
        working days.</li>
        <li><strong>A free consult.</strong> Fifteen minutes for therapy, thirty for supervision
        or EMDR consultation, by Zoom or phone.</li>
        <li><strong>If it is a fit, you get the paperwork.</strong> The
        <a href="/contact/forms/">five client forms</a> and a first appointment. If it is not a
        fit, you get a referral rather than a polite brush-off.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3>Booking an associate instead</h3>
      <p>The practice's <a href="/therapy/associates/">LPC Associates</a> each run their own
      scheduling and billing, and each one has a direct email and phone number on their card.
      Writing to them directly is faster than going through this form. Fees run
      {{ associateStats.individualRange }} a session, with limited sliding-scale places from
      {{ associateStats.slidingFrom }}.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Why this is not a normal web form</h3>
      <p>Ordinary contact forms post your message to a server somewhere. For a counseling
      practice that is the wrong default, so this site does not do it: the form builds an email
      in your own mail app and you decide whether to send it. Nothing reaches a third party, and
      nothing about you is stored here.</p>
      <h3>If this is urgent</h3>
      <p>This practice does not provide emergency care. Call 911 if you are in immediate
      danger, or call or text 988 for the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about booking</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>How long before someone replies?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Usually a couple of working days. Email is the fastest route into the practice, and
      office hours are by appointment rather than fixed, so a reply may not arrive the same
      day.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is the consult really free?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes, and it commits you to nothing. Fifteen minutes for therapy, thirty for supervision
      or EMDR consultation. Its purpose is to work out whether this is the right fit, which
      includes concluding that it is not.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What should I not put in this form?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Clinical detail, diagnoses, and anything you would not want sitting in an ordinary email
      inbox. A sentence about what you are looking for is all that is needed to get a consult
      booked.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I request a specific associate?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes. Say so in the &ldquo;what are you looking for&rdquo; box, or write to them
      directly using the email on their card on the
      <a href="/therapy/associates/">associates page</a>, which is quicker.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  {% include "partials/crisis-note.njk" %}
</section>

